Expose the stored report over the REST API: `@linkchecker` returns it as batched json (with the counts per status a UI needs for its filters), `@linkchecker-csv` serves it as a csv download. Both filter by `status` and `type`, are guarded by the new `rer.linkchecker.ViewReport` permission (`Manager`, `Site Administrator`, `Editor`), and never run a check — they only serve what the last run stored, and report the timestamp it dates from, since a full check takes minutes and is meant to run from cron.
